			<h1>Pipeline Security</h1>
			<p class="subtitle">Transportation Sector Network Management</p>
			
<!-- START putting the Anchor link -->
			
<!-- END putting the Anchor link -->

				
					
							
        				<div class="box" style="text-align: center">
<a href="/what_we_do/tsnm/pipelines/index.shtm">Overview</a> | 
<a href="/what_we_do/tsnm/pipelines/programs.shtm">Initiatives and Programs</a> | 
<a href="/what_we_do/tsnm/pipelines/contact_us.shtm">Senior Staff</a> | 
<a href="/what_we_do/tsnm/pipelines/links.shtm">Links</a> | 
<a href="/what_we_do/tsnm/pipelines/resources.shtm">Resources</a>
</div>

<p><img src="/graphics/images/whatwedo/pipeline_main.jpg" /></p>

					 
      			
					
							
        				<div class="box">
<a href="/what_we_do/tsnm/pipelines/2008_ipsf.shtm"><strong>2008 International Pipeline Security Forum - <font color="#FF0000">Register Now!</font></strong></a>

<p>The 2008 International Pipeline Security Forum will be held on October 29 & 30, 2008, at the Hilton Salt Lake City Center Hotel in Salt Lake City, Utah. <a href="/what_we_do/tsnm/pipelines/2008_ipsf.shtm">Click here</a> for information on the forum, agenda, forum registration, and hotel reservation procedures.</p>
</div>

<div class="box">
<a href="/press/happenings/pipelines_private_firms.shtm">TSA Joins Private Firms in Securing 2.4 Million Miles of Energy Pipelines</a></div>

					 
      			
					
							
									<h2>Mission</h2>
								
						
							
        				<div style="BORDER-RIGHT: #bfcbd4 1px solid; PADDING-RIGHT: 5px; BORDER-TOP: #bfcbd4 1px solid; PADDING-LEFT: 5px; FLOAT: right; PADDING-BOTTOM: 5px; MARGIN: 0px 0px 5px 10px; BORDER-LEFT: #bfcbd4 1px solid; WIDTH: 180px; PADDING-TOP: 5px; BORDER-BOTTOM: #bfcbd4 1px solid; BACKGROUND-COLOR: #ededed; TEXT-ALIGN: left">
<div style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 5px; PADDING-BOTTOM: 5px; BORDER-BOTTOM: #5baacd 1px solid; TEXT-ALIGN: center"><a href="/what_we_do/tsnm/pipelines/cd_brochure.shtm"><img src="/graphics/images/pipeline_cd.gif" border="0" /></a></div>

<center><strong>Pipeline Security<br />
Awareness<br />
CD &amp; Brochures</strong></center>

<p align="center"><a href="/what_we_do/tsnm/pipelines/cd_brochure.shtm">Order Now!</a></p>
</div>

<p>The Pipeline Security Division within our Office of Transportation Sector Network Management (TSNM) has one clear mission &ndash; to enhance the security preparedness of the nation's hazardous liquid and natural gas pipeline systems.</p>

<p>To accomplish this, the division performs several key functions, including:</p>

<ul>
<li>Developing security programs and conducting analysis to maintain pipeline and domain awareness with particular focus on critical systems and infrastructure;</li>

<li>Identifying industry best practices and lessons learned; and,</li>

<li>Maintaining a dynamic modal network through&nbsp;effective communications with the pipeline industry and government stakeholders.</li>
</ul>


					
							
						 
      			
					
							
									<h2>The Pipeline System Landscape in the U.S.</h2>
								
						
							
        				<p>The national pipeline system is an extensive mode of transportation with unique infrastructure security characteristics and requirements. Virtually all the critical pipeline infrastructure is owned or operated by private entities. There are:</p>

<ul>
<li>161,189 miles of hazardous liquid pipelines operated by over 200 operators</li>

<li>309,503 miles of natural gas transmission pipelines operated by over 700 operators</li>

<li>1.9 million miles of natural gas distribution pipelines operated by over 1300 operators</li>
</ul>

<a id="forum" name="forum"></a>

					
							
						 
      			
	
